# Commits skipped by `git blame`: these changed formatting or line endings
# only, never behaviour, so blaming them buries whoever wrote the code.
#
# Enable locally, once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub's web blame reads this file automatically -- no configuration there.
#
# NOTE: list the SHA as it exists on `main`, not the branch SHA. This repo
# squash-merges, so the commit that lands on main is a new object and a branch
# SHA recorded here would never match. Add the entry after the merge.

